Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:36:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] ttf: read glyph categories

Categories were left unset, so a compiler guessed them from glyph names. Now
they follow GDEF's glyph classes. A font without them gets none either (every
glyph a base), unless it attaches marks: a compiler then writes classes anyway,
so a glyph a shaper would take for a mark is one.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
